Explanation:

Dissolution produces carbonic acid, releasing $H^+$ ($CO_2 + H_2O arrow.r.l H^+ + HCO_3^-$). Free $H^+$ consumes carbonate ions ($H^+ + CO_3^(2-) arrow.r.l HCO_3^-$), reducing the saturation state for calcifiers.
